<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Nan Ya 1996 sales down 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Nan Ya 1996 sales down 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nan Ya Plastics Corp, Taiwan's largest private industrial firm, said on Wednesday its sales revenues in 1996 fell 2.9 percent to T$88.865 billion from T$91.494 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>In the month of December, the firm's sales increased 5.8 percent to T$8.131 billion from T$7.685 billion in December 1995, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement did not provide profit figures.</p>
<p>Nan Ya said it did not reach its initial 1996 sales target of T$98.35 billion, but gave no explanation.</p>
<p>Nan Ya is a key member of Formosa Plastics group.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
